# Git flow

- `main` is the integration branch. Do not commit feature work directly on `main`.
- One branch per product-scope item: `feature/<short-slug>` (example: `feature/connect-ldap`).
- Branch from current `main`. Do not stack unrelated work on one branch.
- Commit on the feature branch (why, not what). No `--no-verify`, no `git config` changes, no force-push to `main`.
- When the item is done: `git checkout main` then `git merge --no-ff feature/<slug>`.
- Do not open a PR or push unless asked.
- Never mix LDAP writes, Entra, or a fifth workspace onto a UI-polish branch.
